  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9266273b8f123004195741f969177dda, type: 3}
  title: Gameplay
  sections:
  - heading: Features
    text: "Features are the main types that define the behaviours of any gameplay
      elements. Features are C# types that don't derive from MonoBehaviour, but that
      derive from Feature. They are meant to be lightweight, as independant as possible,
      and should work by composition (see \u2192 components)"
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Components
    text: Components are MonoBehaviours that work by composition. They store various
      features, and implement the interface IFeatureCollection. The benefit of using
      features and components is that we only program things once, and can reuse
      them easily without copy-pasting code.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Data
    text: Mostly ScriptableObjects, see the readme inside the data folder
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Upgrades
    text: ToDO
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
